{
  "//": [
    "Canonical Node ops-api dependency fragment (#936).",
    "",
    "This is a package.json FRAGMENT, not a package file: merge these blocks into",
    "your service's own package.json, then `npm install`. It is the Node analogue",
    "of the Go payload's go.mod.deps, the Python payload's requirements.txt and the",
    "Java payload's build.gradle.kts dependency block. Comments ride in this `//`",
    "key -- npm's own convention for annotating a package.json -- so the file stays",
    "valid JSON that jq and npm can both read.",
    "",
    "YOUR package.json MUST DECLARE \"type\": \"module\". opsApi.ts is NodeNext ESM and",
    "reads `import.meta.url` to find your package.json for the /info version",
    "fallback; under CommonJS that is a compile error, not a runtime surprise --",
    "which is the good outcome, but it is the one adoption step nothing else names.",
    "",
    "OpenTelemetry-only instrumentation, per ARCHITECTURE.md: the OTel SDK is the",
    "single metrics source. The Prometheus exporter serves the /metrics pull-compat",
    "surface; the two OTLP exporters are the PRIMARY push pipeline, wired only when",
    "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT (or OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_METRICS_ENDPOINT) is set.",
    "BOTH exporters are required because OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL (or its",
    "_METRICS_ twin) selects grpc or http/protobuf at RUNTIME -- dropping one turns",
    "a config value into a build error.",
    "",
    "NO WEB FRAMEWORK APPEARS HERE, and none may be added: the payload's HTTP layer",
    "is node:http, so it drops into an Express service, a Fastify service and a",
    "service with no framework alike. Nor any circuit-breaker library -- the",
    "dependency-health seam is an interface, and #1145 is what implements it.",
    "",
    "Versions are a floor, not a pin -- Renovate/Dependabot move them. Read the",
    "three @opentelemetry/* lines below as THREE independent release trains, not",
    "one: this is upstream's own versioning, and every one of the three majors",
    "here is deliberate.",
    "",
    "  1. @opentelemetry/api is on its own 1.x line and stays there -- the API",
    "     package is versioned separately from the SDK, and there is no 2.x to",
    "     move it to. Do NOT bump it to match sdk-metrics for the sake of",
    "     coherence; that version does not exist.",
    "  2. @opentelemetry/sdk-metrics is on the SDK's 2.x line.",
    "  3. The three exporter-* packages are on a shared 0.x line -- upstream's",
    "     versioning for the still-experimental metrics exporters, not a mistake.",
    "     Those three MUST move TOGETHER: they are one release train, and a mixed",
    "     set fails at runtime on an API mismatch. tests/ops-api-language-",
    "     payloads.bats asserts that coherence.",
    "",
    "@types/node's MAJOR must match the Node major your service RUNS. This file",
    "ships 24, the scaffold's own default. Adopting into a repo that already has",
    "a runtime pin: lower or raise this entry to THAT pin. The README beside this",
    "file states the source precedence in full -- do not restate it here, so there",
    "is one copy to keep true.",
    "Typing against a newer major than you run is silently wrong: tsc accepts APIs",
    "that are absent at runtime, so the failure lands in production rather than in",
    "the build.",
    "",
    "The payload's own Node floor is ^18.19.0 || >=20.6.0 -- the engines.node the",
    "sdk-metrics and exporter-* packages below declare. Below it these packages do",
    "not install at all."
  ],
  "type": "module",
  "dependencies": {
    "@opentelemetry/api": "^1.9.1",
    "@opentelemetry/exporter-metrics-otlp-grpc": "^0.221.0",
    "@opentelemetry/exporter-metrics-otlp-proto": "^0.221.0",
    "@opentelemetry/exporter-prometheus": "^0.221.0",
    "@opentelemetry/sdk-metrics": "^2.10.0"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@types/node": "^24.10.0"
  }
}
